[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MikalaiKryvusha/Kriniks_Conan_Exiles_Enhanced_ModPack/main/_config/branding/krinik-modpack-logo.webp[/img][/center]
[center][size=4][b][i]Krinik Mod Pack 0.9.0 · Conan Exiles Enhanced 3.0.1[/i][/b][/size][/center]
[center][color=#D4D4D8]English below · Русский текст — после английского[/color][/center]
[line]
[size=6][b]EN[/b][/size]

[size=5][b]• Description[/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]Krinik Mod Pack 0.9.0 turns [b][i]Conan Exiles Enhanced 3.0.1[/i][/b] into an old-school role-playing game in the spirit of [b][i]The Elder Scrolls IV: Oblivion[/i][/b]. The pack brings together 7 mods by its author and 64 mods by other authors from the Steam Workshop and Nexus Mods, tuned to work together, with the UE4SS loader and a launcher. The camera stands behind the hero's back, the arrow flies along an arc to the aim point, and the hero grows up to level 10,000, running faster, jumping higher and shooting better with every level. The inventory and the hub pause the game, so loot can be sorted at leisure. The world is larger and more dangerous: new lands and dungeons, ambushes, night demons and undead, storms, heat and cold, and over 700 new NPCs. At home a settlement with its own daily routine waits for the hero, and on the road a party of up to a hundred followers marches with the hero. The base is run from all its chests at once, and thousands of decor items furnish it. The interface is reworked for readability and gets a HUD, a minimap, a damage meter and follower health bars.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b]The pack is made for the Russian version of the game:[/b] every mod is translated into Russian, and the pack switches the game to Russian. The launcher installs, launches and removes the pack, and the «Отзыв» (Feedback) button in the game menu collects a report for the author. Version 0.9.0 ships as the pack worked on 2 November 2026; what is not done yet is listed below and goes into 1.0.0.[/color]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MikalaiKryvusha/Kriniks_Conan_Exiles_Enhanced_ModPack/main/docs/nexus/hero_oasis_0_9_0.webp[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]• Main features[/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]Full Russian localization[/size][/b]
All mods in this collection are fully localized into Russian, using the same terminology as the base game. This includes mod settings menus, in-game messages, religious abilities, the settlement log, and fish names.[/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]
[b][size=4]Camera positioning controls[/size][/b]
The third-person camera follows the classic design principles of 2000s-era RPGs: the character is viewed strictly from behind, and players can adjust the camera’s position to suit their own preferences directly in-game using the numeric keypad. Features include saving the camera’s position, resetting it to default, and restoring a previously saved player preset.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]Archery mechanics[/size][/b]
Archery has been fundamentally overhauled, drawing inspiration from classic 2000s RPGs to ensure the character handles a bow like a true archer. Much like in [b][i]The Elder Scrolls IV: Oblivion[/i][/b], arrows travel along an arc toward the crosshair, with flight speed determined by the draw strength. The system includes a first-person view while holding a bow, refined camera behavior for easier aiming in both first- and third-person perspectives, and the ability to fire while jumping.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]Character progression up to level 10,000[/size][/b]
The game features a virtually infinite leveling system, allowing for continuous character growth. This progression directly impacts the character’s abilities in tangible ways—such as faster running, higher and longer jumps, improved archery skills, and more.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]Pausing in the inventory and hub[/size][/b]
The game automatically pauses when you open your inventory or hub, giving you the time to calmly sort through your loot and plan your next moves.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]Settlement and Companions[/size][/b]
The hero’s base operates on its own schedule: thralls sleep, eat, work, train, trade, and go on patrol. When the hero travels, they are accompanied by a retinue of up to a hundred followers, with thralls riding alongside them. It is possible to capture bosses and unique characters as thralls, and they can level up to rank 50.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]New Lands[/size][/b]
Beyond the horizon lie new locations: the Caves of Set, home to the Akhlut Outpost; a Shemite city-state in the western savannah; the Ymir’s Respite dungeon, featuring a boss arena; and the restored fortress of Al-Merayah. A network of map-rooms (waystones) has been implemented to allow for fast travel across the world map.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]A Dangerous World[/size][/b]
Beyond the walls of your base, ambushes await. At night, demons and the undead emerge from the darkness, while harsh weather—including storms, extreme heat, and bitter cold—forces the hero to seek shelter. Over 700 new NPCs from the world’s native factions have been added, along with dark, treacherous dungeons.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]Gear and Appearance[/size][/b]
Tailor your hero’s equipment and appearance to fit their backstory: the game features weapons with unique attack combos, armor sets representing seven different religions, a rune system, a "glory" (reputation) mechanic, new hairstyles, and character designs based on the descriptions by Robert E. Howard.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]Base Management and Daily Life[/size][/b]
Manage your base efficiently without having to check every chest individually: the game supports building and crafting using resources stored anywhere in your base. Features include automated inventory sorting into chests, a dedicated "sorter" chest, and doubled storage capacity. Additionally, fishing—complete with fish traps—and thousands of decorative items allow you to furnish your home exactly as you wish.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]User Interface[/size][/b]
Extensive work has been carried out to fix flaws across various elements of the graphical user interface, improving usability and readability, resolving defects, and ensuring a consistent visual style in line with [b][i]Conan Exiles[/i][/b]. Additions include a customizable "Hosav's HUD," a minimap, a damage counter, health bars for companions, and an FPS counter.[/color]

[color=#D4D4D8][b][size=4]Launcher and Feedback[/size][/b]
The [i][b]KrinikConanLauncher.exe[/b][/i] launcher now supports installing the mod pack, launching the game, accessing the user manual, generating a report for the author, and uninstalling the pack (restoring the game to its pre-installation state). A [b][Feedback][/b] button has been added to both the main menu and the [b][ESC][/b] menu; it generates a report and opens an email to the pack author.[/color]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MikalaiKryvusha/Kriniks_Conan_Exiles_Enhanced_ModPack/main/docs/nexus/cover_0_9_0.webp[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]• Pack contents[/b][/size]

[color=#D4D4D8]The pack holds 7 mods by its author, the UE4SS loader and 64 mods by other authors. [color=#E0A458]KRINIK MODIFIED[/color] marks mods by other authors that were changed for the pack: Russian translation, interface fixes, bug fixes. Every name links to the mod's page.[/color]

